<p>Some applications allow the page size and orientation of a single document 
 to be changed. When documents containing a mixture of landscape and portrait 
 pages are printed, document pages whose orientation differs from the paper 
 orientation are printed rotated by 90 degrees. You can change the direction 
 in which the images are rotated. </p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Printer Defaults</span>, 
 you can specify the print direction settings even when layout-printing 
 or booklet-printing is selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu. When you apply layout-printing or booklet-printing to documents 
 containing a mixture of landscape and portrait pages, document pages whose 
 orientation differs from the paper orientation are rotated or not rotated 
 but reduced in size. Therefore, no blank pages are output.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Output Settings</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate Mixed Original 
 Orientation...</span> to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate Mixed Original 
 Orientation</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Printer Defaults</span>,<span class="Term-Soft"> Rotate to a naturally readable direction</span>, or <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate to reverse readable direction</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
